<title>UK: London tea auction sees improved all-round demand.</title>
<headline>London tea auction sees improved all-round demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monday's landed tea auction saw improved general demand, the official report said.</p>
<p>Prices for selected Best Assams were firmer on good competition.</p>
<p>Coloury mediums were steady but plainer types tended lower while East Africans were fully firm.</p>
<p>An offering of 800 packages offshore teas met with good demand at firm-to-dearer rates, the report said.</p>
<p>The next auction is on October 28.</p>
<p>-Lonodn Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
</text>
